        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1e293b&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;What happens, in order, when a project admin restores an app database from the CMP?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: one app with backups enabled on the K3s hub · main as of 2026-10-29 · derived from code (CMP security_databases.py, services/security/restore.py, RestoreDialog.tsx; infra-templates cnpg-cluster.yaml, values.yaml)&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: EKS and GKE (backups not wired, CNP-165) · how the browser reaches the CMP (Cloudflare, Envoy) · the backup itself (see app-backup)&lt;br&gt;Arrows: plain = request, dashed = reply. A restore never touches the running database: it builds &amp;lt;app&amp;gt;-db-r&amp;lt;N+1&amp;gt; beside it. The confirm call repeats the reads of the dry run.&lt;br&gt;v0.1 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
